Derivative of Exponential Functions
f(x)=e^{ax+b}
f′(x)=ae^{ax+b}

f(x) = 2^x = e^{(log_e 2^x)}
             = e^{x log_e 2}

f′(x) = (log_e 2)e^{x log_e 2}
        = (ln 2) · 2^x

f(x) = 2^x = e^{(log_e 2^x)}
             = e^{x log_e 2}

f′(x) = (log_e 2)e^{x log_e 2}
        = (ln 2) · 2^x

Every positive real number can be written with base e: a = e^{ln a}
Every exponential function can be written with base e: a^x = e^{x ln a}
To differentiate exponential functions of any base:
f(x) = a^x
f′(x) = (ln a) a^x
